From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 15:06:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] allocator_dma_heap: force default_cma_region for mainline 7.1
 + rcawston VEPU580

Mainline exposes /dev/dma_heap/{system,default_cma_region,reserved}, not the
Rockchip-BSP heap names. The VEPU580 needs a physically contiguous bitstream
buffer (the rcawston driver does not coalesce a multi-segment dma-buf import
into one IOVA range). Point every heap_infos entry at the contiguous
default_cma_region heap so hevc_rkmpp/h264_rkmpp encode works against the
stock kernel.

That heap hands out a cached mapping, so every entry is marked cacheable too.
An entry claiming MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_NONE describes memory MPP will not issue
DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC for, which is a false statement about this heap. The
encoder's own stream buffer is that case: mpp_enc_check_pkt_buf() takes it
from a MPP_BUFFER_TYPE_ION group with no cacheable flag, so the parameter sets
and SEI the CPU writes and the slice data the VPU writes share one buffer with
no cache maintenance between them. The packet is the right length and
structurally invalid -- at every IDR the four bytes holding the slice start
code carry unrelated data, the slice is swallowed by the preceding NAL, and
the picture is lost. Measured on RK3588 at 1280x720, 90 frames, gop 12: 24 of
90 h264 frames and 11 of 90 hevc frames decoded back before, 90 of 90 after.

Local patch -- not for upstream. Revert if pairing with a BSP kernel.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 osal/allocator/allocator_dma_heap.c | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/osal/allocator/allocator_dma_heap.c b/osal/allocator/allocator_dma_heap.c
index b08cc7c..cb50f99 100644
--- a/osal/allocator/allocator_dma_heap.c
+++ b/osal/allocator/allocator_dma_heap.c
@@ -62,15 +62,51 @@ typedef struct DmaHeapInfo_t {
     RK_U32      flags;
 } DmaHeapInfo;
 
+/*
+ * LOCAL PATCH (rockchip-accel, mainline 7.1 + rcawston VEPU580):
+ *
+ * Every heap is "default_cma_region", the mainline kernel's
+ * CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_CMA heap on this board, and every heap is cacheable.
+ *
+ * The name, because mainline exposes /dev/dma_heap/{system,
+ * default_cma_region,reserved} and none of the Rockchip-BSP names (cma,
+ * system-dma32, system-uncached, ...). With the upstream table only "system"
+ * opens, so the encoder gets a page-allocator buffer; the rcawston VEPU580
+ * driver's dma-buf import does not coalesce a multi-segment import into one
+ * IOVA range, its guardrail then rejects the bitstream-top register (BSBT),
+ * and past that the encoder would IOMMU-fault writing across IOVA gaps.
+ * default_cma_region is physically contiguous, hence a single IOVA range.
+ *
+ * The flags, because that heap hands out a cached mapping. An entry that
+ * claims MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_NONE describes memory MPP will not issue
+ * DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC for, and the CPU-written and VPU-written parts of such a
+ * buffer never become coherent. The encoder's own stream buffer is exactly
+ * that case -- mpp_enc_check_pkt_buf() takes it from a MPP_BUFFER_TYPE_ION
+ * group with no cacheable flag -- so the parameter sets and SEI written by the
+ * CPU and the slice data written by the VPU land in one buffer with no cache
+ * maintenance between them. The packet is the right length and structurally
+ * invalid: at every IDR the four bytes holding the slice start code carry
+ * unrelated data, the slice is swallowed by the preceding NAL, and the picture
+ * is lost. Measured on RK3588 at 1280x720, 90 frames, gop 12: 24 of 90 h264
+ * frames and 11 of 90 hevc frames decoded back before this, 90 of 90 after.
+ *
+ * The DMA32 and CMA bits are left as the index describes them; only the
+ * cacheable bit was a false statement about the memory.
+ *
+ * MPP here is encode-only (decode uses v4l2request), so the extra CMA pressure
+ * is modest. If 4K needs more, grow the CMA reservation via bootarg/DT `cma=`,
+ * not a kernel rebuild. Revert this block to the upstream BSP heap names if
+ * ever pairing with a Rockchip BSP kernel.
+ */
 static DmaHeapInfo heap_infos[MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_TYPE_NB] = {
-    {   "system-uncached",          -1,                                                MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_NONE , },   /* 0 */
-    {   "system-uncached-dma32",    -1,                                                MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_DMA32, },   /* 1 */
-    {   "system",                   -1,                      MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE                       , },   /* 2 */
-    {   "system-dma32",             -1,                      MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_DMA32, },   /* 3 */
-    {   "cma-uncached",             -1, MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CMA                                                 , },   /* 4 */
-    {   "cma-uncached-dma32",       -1, MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CMA                           | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_DMA32, },   /* 5 */
-    {   "cma",                      -1, MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CMA | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE                       , },   /* 6 */
-    {   "cma-dma32",                -1, MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CMA | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_DMA32, },   /* 7 */
+    {   "default_cma_region",       -1,                      MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE                       , },   /* 0 */
+    {   "default_cma_region",       -1,                      MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_DMA32, },   /* 1 */
+    {   "default_cma_region",       -1,                      MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE                       , },   /* 2 */
+    {   "default_cma_region",       -1,                      MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_DMA32, },   /* 3 */
+    {   "default_cma_region",       -1, MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CMA | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE                       , },   /* 4 */
+    {   "default_cma_region",       -1, MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CMA | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_DMA32, },   /* 5 */
+    {   "default_cma_region",       -1, MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CMA | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE                       , },   /* 6 */
+    {   "default_cma_region",       -1, MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CMA | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_CACHABLE | MPP_ALLOC_FLAG_DMA32, },   /* 7 */
 };
 
 static int try_open_path(const char *name)
